/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock IS committed — this workspace ships a binary.

# Never commit real authentication material, even hashed.
tokens.json
*.tokens.json
!*/tests/fixtures/*-tokens.json

# Controller inventory carries site names and controller addresses.
controllers.json
!*/tests/fixtures/*-controllers.json

.env
.DS_Store

# subagent-driven-development scratch
.superpowers/

# Local UniFi API key — never commit. mecmcp-secret requires mode 0600.
.unifikey
*.unifikey
.unifi-api-key

# Recorded controller fixtures are captured from a live controller and are
# deliberately not published. A fresh clone has none. Regenerate with
# scripts/capture-fixtures.sh against a live controller.
#
# The `synthetic/` set is the exception: it is hand-written, carries no real
# network data, and is committed so the parser, workflow and change-set tests
# run on a fresh clone and in CI. `gate_passes_on_the_committed_synthetic_fixtures`
# holds it to the same scrub gate the recorded sets must pass.
rustunifimcp-core/tests/fixtures/*/
!rustunifimcp-core/tests/fixtures/synthetic/
!rustunifimcp-core/tests/fixtures/README.md

# Real fixture denylist is local-only (contains the identifiers it protects).
scripts/fixture-denylist.txt
